  "audience": "tech",
  "body": "| | |\n| :-- | :-- |\n| **Document ID** | DOC-SAF-003 |\n| **Version** | 1.1 |\n| **Effective date** | November 2026 |\n| **Owner** | Safety Lead |\n| **Use** | Field tailboard — completed by the PM/Lead with the crew before work starts, every site, every day. Keep with the job record. |\n\n**Project / site:** ______________________ **Date:** ____________\n\n**PM / Lead:** ______________________ **Crew present:** ______________________\n\n## Stop-work authority\n\n☐ Everyone briefed: **anyone may stop the job at any time if the risk is unclear or unsafe.**\n\n## 1. Job basics\n\n☐ Scope of work explained\n☐ Roles assigned and understood\n☐ Permits / drawings reviewed\n\nNotes: ______________________\n\n## 2. Hazards (check all that apply)\n\n☐ Electrical / live power\n☐ Heights / ladders / lifts\n☐ Confined spaces\n☐ Heavy lifting / material handling\n☐ Slip / trip / fall\n☐ Tools / equipment\n☐ Other: ______________________\n\n## 3. Controls & safety checks\n\n☐ PPE worn (glasses, gloves, hard hat, vest)\n☐ LOTO in place if needed (DOC-SAF-002)\n☐ Ladders / lifts inspected\n☐ First aid kit and fire extinguisher available\n☐ Work area clean and organized\n☐ Emergency exits clear\n\nNotes: ______________________\n\n## 4. Emergency readiness\n\n☐ CPR-trained person identified: ______________________\n☐ Nearest medical facility known\n☐ Incident reporting reviewed (report to the COO and Safety Lead immediately)\n\nNotes: ______________________\n\n## 5. Team confirmation\n\n☐ Everyone understands the scope, hazards and controls\n☐ Everyone agrees to stop work if unsafe\n\n**Crew signatures:** ______________________\n\n**PM / Lead sign-off:** ______________________\n\n## Revision History\n\n| Version | Date | Changes | Author | Approved by |\n| :-: | :-: | :-- | :-- | :-- |\n| 1.0 | 2025 | Initial release (was numbered DOC-SAF-007 / DOC-SAF-PJRA-002) | COO | CEO |\n| 1.1 | 11/2026 | Single ID DOC-SAF-003; formatting cleaned up | Corey Williams (COO) | Daniel Aaron (CEO) |"
